    "summary": "This metric evaluates the consistency of environmental atmosphere (color-temperature logic) in generated videos. We analyze the Hue channel in HSV color space: the hue spectrum $[0, 179]$ is divided into $7$ core intervals to construct a hue feature vector $\\mathbf{h} t \\in \\mathbb{R}^{7}$. We then compute a weighted perceptual similarity of the full sequence relative to the initial frame. To balance global constancy and local transition , the similarity at frame $t$ ($t \\geq 2$) is the arithmetic mean of current-to-first and current-to-previous similarities. The similarity $S(\\cdot, \\cdot)$ follows the cosine inner product (same as Eq. (3) in the brightness-distribution metric): \\[ S(a, b) = \\frac{a \\cdot b}{\\|a\\|\\,\\|b\\|} = \\frac{\\sum {i=1}^{n} a i b i}{ \\sqrt{\\sum {i=1}^{n} a i^2}\\,\\sqrt{\\sum {i=1}^{n} b i^2} } \\tag{3} \\] \\[ \\bar{S} t = \\frac{ S(\\mathbf{h} t, \\mathbf{h} 1) + S(\\mathbf{h} t, \\mathbf{h} {t-1}) }{ 2 } \\tag{7} \\] For each frame $I t$, RGB is converted to HSV; a saturation-weighted histogram over $7$ hue bins on $[0, 180)$ is normalized to form $\\mathbf{h} t$ (WorldArena default hue bins=7). The final score uses a normalized exponentially decaying weighted sum , where weights $\\hat{w}'(d)$ are an improved variant of $\\hat{w}(d)$ with faster decay ($\\beta \\alpha$), and similarities are passed through the modified Softmax transform $T(\\cdot)$ (Eq. (4), default $\\lambda = 4.0$): \\[ T(x) = \\frac{e^{\\lambda x} - 1}{e^{\\lambda} - 1}, \\quad \\lambda 0 \\tag{4} \\] \\[ w'(d) = e^{-\\beta \\cdot d}, \\qquad \\hat{w}'(d) = \\frac{w'(d)}{\\sum {k=1}^{T-1} w'(k)} \\quad (\\beta 0) \\tag{8} \\] Here $d \\in [1, T-1]$ is the frame distance ($d=1$ for the second frame relative to the first), and $\\beta$ is the decay coefficient. The default $\\beta = 0.10$ exceeds the brightness metric's $\\alpha = 0.05$, so $\\hat{w}'(d)$ decays faster than $\\hat{w}(d)$ and long-video color drift is penalized more strongly. The comprehensive score is: \\[ S {\\mathrm{Color}} = \\sum {d=1}^{T-1} \\hat{w}'(d) \\cdot T\\!\\left(\\bar{S} {d+1}\\right) \\tag{9} \\] In WorldArena this algorithm is implemented as the official metric color temperature constraint (hue distribution backend). Under the default normalization config, raw and normalized outputs lie in $[0,1]$ with higher is better . The legacy scalar alias color temperature consistency remains diagnostic and is not part of the seven-metric official quality total.",
