    "route": "/doc/benchmark/metrics/temporal-flickering/",
    "summary": "Temporal Flickering quantifies inter-frame pixel stability in a generated video. High-frequency brightness or color shifts between consecutive frames produce visible flicker; this metric penalizes such instability using mean absolute error (MAE) on RGB pixels. Given $N$ decoded frames $\\{x i\\} {i=1}^{N}$, the per-pair pixel MAE is \\[ \\mathrm{MAE}(x i, x {i+1}) = \\frac{1}{HWC}\\sum {h,w,c}\\left|x i(h,w,c)-x {i+1}(h,w,c)\\right| \\tag{1} \\] where $H$, $W$, and $C$ are height, width, and channel count. WorldArena evaluates MAE on uint8 RGB values in $[0,255]$. When resolutions differ, the later frame is resized to match the earlier frame before differencing. The temporal flickering score aggregates adjacent-frame MAE: \\[ S {\\mathrm{flick}} = \\frac{255 - \\frac{1}{N-1}\\sum {i=1}^{N-1}\\mathrm{MAE}(x i, x {i+1})}{255} \\tag{2} \\] Higher $S {\\mathrm{flick}}$ indicates less flicker. The metric is prediction-only and requires at least two frames. Verified Same-Input Temporal Flickering Example This page keeps one case only. Both video first frames pass geometric matching against the displayed input; scores illustrate this metric only, not overall model ranking. Machine-readable audit manifest. Input image Verified case · adjacent-pixel MAE is motion-sensitive image static photorealistic living spaces 0140 image static photorealistic / indoor / living spaces Benchmark prompt target Camera push in. A living room with sofa, bookshelf, and books. Output A moves little, while Output B makes a larger smooth camera move and reveals the bookshelf. The lower score for Output B reflects larger pixel changes; by itself it does not prove visible high-frequency flicker because this implementation is not motion-compensated. Output A Temporal Flickering: 0.9634 · mean pairwise MAE 9.3268 Output B Temporal Flickering: 0.7694 · mean pairwise MAE 58.8134",
    "tags": [
      "Benchmark",
      "metrics"
    ],
    "content": "# Temporal Flickering\n\nTemporal Flickering quantifies **inter-frame pixel stability** in a generated video. High-frequency brightness or color shifts between consecutive frames produce visible flicker; this metric penalizes such instability using mean absolute error (MAE) on RGB pixels.\n\nGiven $N$ decoded frames $\\{x_i\\}_{i=1}^{N}$, the per-pair pixel MAE is\n\n\\[\n\\mathrm{MAE}(x_i, x_{i+1})\n=\n\\frac{1}{HWC}\\sum_{h,w,c}\\left|x_i(h,w,c)-x_{i+1}(h,w,c)\\right|\n\\tag{1}\n\\]\n\nwhere $H$, $W$, and $C$ are height, width, and channel count. WorldArena evaluates MAE on uint8 RGB values in $[0,255]$. When resolutions differ, the later frame is resized to match the earlier frame before differencing.\n\nThe temporal flickering score aggregates adjacent-frame MAE:\n\n\\[\nS_{\\mathrm{flick}}\n=\n\\frac{255 - \\frac{1}{N-1}\\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\\mathrm{MAE}(x_i, x_{i+1})}{255}\n\\tag{2}\n\\]\n\nHigher $S_{\\mathrm{flick}}$ indicates less flicker. The metric is **prediction-only** and requires at least two frames.\n\n<!-- temporal-flickering-representative-cases:start -->\n## Verified Same-Input Temporal Flickering Example\n\nThis page keeps one case only. Both video first frames pass geometric matching against the displayed input; scores illustrate this metric only, not overall model ranking.\n\n[Machine-readable audit manifest](/assets/worldarena/assets/metric_examples/temporal_flickering_representative_manifest.csv).\n\n<div class=\"metric-case-stack\">\n<article class=\"metric-case-exhibit\">\n  <div class=\"metric-case-context\">\n    <figure class=\"metric-input-card\">\n      <img src=\"/assets/worldarena/assets/metric_examples/inputs/c857427716ae__image_static_photorealistic_living_spaces_0140.jpg\" alt=\"Input image: image_static_photorealistic_living_spaces_0140\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n      <figcaption>Input image</figcaption>\n    </figure>\n    <div class=\"metric-case-copy\">\n      <div class=\"metric-case-kicker\">Verified case · adjacent-pixel MAE is motion-sensitive</div>\n      <h4><code>image_static_photorealistic_living_spaces_0140</code></h4>\n      <div class=\"metric-case-meta\"><span>image_static</span><span>photorealistic / indoor / living_spaces</span></div>\n      <div class=\"metric-case-prompt\">\n        <span>Benchmark prompt target</span>\n        <p>Camera push in. A living room with sofa, bookshelf, and books.</p>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"metric-case-note\">Output A moves little, while Output B makes a larger smooth camera move and reveals the bookshelf. The lower score for Output B reflects larger pixel changes; by itself it does not prove visible high-frequency flicker because this implementation is not motion-compensated.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"metric-output-grid\">\n    <figure class=\"metric-output-card\">\n      <div class=\"metric-output-media-wrap\">\n        <video class=\"metric-output-video\" controls muted loop playsinline preload=\"metadata\" aria-label=\"Output A: ac3d-image-static, living space 0140\">\n          <source src=\"/assets/worldarena/assets/metric_examples/3a76d4fa805b__ac3d-image-static__image_static_photorealistic_living_spaces_0140.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\">\n        </video>\n      </div>\n      <figcaption class=\"metric-output-caption\">\n        <strong>Output A</strong>\n        <span>Temporal Flickering: <strong>0.9634</strong> · mean pairwise MAE 9.3268</span>\n      </figcaption>\n    </figure>\n    <figure class=\"metric-output-card\">\n      <div class=\"metric-output-media-wrap\">\n        <video class=\"metric-output-video\" controls muted loop playsinline preload=\"metadata\" aria-label=\"Output B: LongCat-Video, living space 0140\">\n          <source src=\"/assets/worldarena/assets/metric_examples/d43209bc4d20__longcat-video-image-static-8gpu-20260612_133950__image_static_photorealistic_living_spaces_0140.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\">\n        </video>\n      </div>\n      <figcaption class=\"metric-output-caption\">\n        <strong>Output B</strong>\n        <span>Temporal Flickering: <strong>0.7694</strong> · mean pairwise MAE 58.8134</span>\n      </figcaption>\n    </figure>\n  </div>\n</article>\n</div>\n<!-- temporal-flickering-representative-cases:end -->\n\n## References {#reference}\n\n!!! quote \"VBench — Temporal Flickering (Appendix C.2.3)\"\n\n    Consecutive-frame pixel MAE converted to a $[0,1]$ stability score via $(255 - \\overline{\\mathrm{MAE}})/255$.\n"
